Lantern (called Hermlet up to version 0.1) is an independent community
project. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by or supported by Nous
Research. "Hermes", "Hermes Agent" and "Nous Research" are names of Nous
Research and are used here only to describe what this software works with.

Where ideas came from
---------------------

* Muse Gadgets (https://github.com/facebookincubator/muse-gadget-sdk, Apache
  2.0) for the shape of the original project: a device you put on a spare
  Linux box, with a README for people and an AGENTS.md for coding agents. No
  code from it is used.

* Hermes Gadget (https://github.com/Adolanium/hermes-gadget-sdk, MIT) inspired
  the optional platform plugin of earlier versions. That plugin has been
  removed from this version; it remains in the project's history.

Bundled into the screen's UI when it is built, each under its own licence
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

* Preact (https://preactjs.com), MIT.
* markdown-it (https://github.com/markdown-it/markdown-it), MIT.
* DOMPurify (https://github.com/cure53/DOMPurify), Apache 2.0 or MPL 2.0.
* highlight.js (https://highlightjs.org), BSD 3-Clause.
* qrcode-generator (https://github.com/kazuhikoarase/qrcode-generator), MIT.
* Inter (https://rsms.me/inter/) and JetBrains Mono
  (https://www.jetbrains.com/lp/mono/) fonts, SIL Open Font License 1.1, via
  Fontsource.

Installed on the device from Raspberry Pi OS, each under its own licence
------------------------------------------------------------------------

* cage, Chromium, Plymouth, PipeWire and Noto Color Emoji.
* websockets (https://github.com/python-websockets/websockets), BSD 3-Clause,
  the service's only Python dependency.
